def education(clv=False):
 cs=deepcopy(COMMON)
 if not clv:return cs
 # The uploaded glioma guide is not a diagnosis or treatment reference for CLV.
 cs[0]={'id':'embryonal-diagnosis','title':'Understanding your particular brain tumour','intro':'CLV here is for selected adult high-risk medulloblastoma or another eligible embryonal tumour; it is not a glioma regimen.','items':[
 item('The exact diagnosis matters','Medulloblastoma is an embryonal tumour that usually starts in the cerebellum. The NCCP regimen also names other primitive neuro-ectodermal tumours, including pinealoblastoma. Ask the specialist to record the current pathology name and explain any older wording. These diagnoses are not interchangeable with glioblastoma or other gliomas.',['nccp','nci-medulloblastoma']),
 item('Risk group and spread','The team considers the exact tumour, what remains after surgery and whether it has spread within the brain, spine or cerebrospinal fluid. Ask what makes your tumour high risk and which results establish that. A general glioma grade explanation does not replace medulloblastoma risk assessment.',['nccp','nci-medulloblastoma']),
 item('Molecular results','Medulloblastoma can be classified by molecular findings, including WNT, SHH and non-WNT/non-SHH groups. Ask which tests apply to your exact tumour and how they affect discussion. Molecular tests used for another tumour type are not automatically relevant to this diagnosis. If a result is pending or not applicable, record that clearly.',['nci-medulloblastoma']),
 item('How the treatments fit together','Surgery obtains tissue and removes tumour where safely possible. Craniospinal radiotherapy treats planned areas of the brain and spine. This NCCP CLV schedule starts four to six weeks after craniospinal RT, after recovery and safety review. The team confirms the role of each part for your diagnosis.',['nccp','nci-medulloblastoma']),
 item('A useful diagnosis record','Keep the pathology date and wording, risk group and its reasons, molecular results if relevant, surgery and RT dates, brain/spine scan findings and any cerebrospinal-fluid assessment. Ask who will explain pending results. Use this record to understand decisions, not to determine your own chemotherapy eligibility.',['nccp','nci-medulloblastoma'])]}
 cs[1]={'id':'embryonal-tests','title':'Tests, scans and recovery after treatment','intro':'Safety tests and tumour-response tests have different purposes.','items':[
 item('Bloods, kidneys and hydration','Blood counts check marrow recovery; kidney and liver tests help assess whether treatment is safe. Cisplatin also needs an individual hydration and electrolyte plan. Tell staff about fluid restrictions, swelling, heart or kidney problems and difficulty drinking. Do not use a generic home fluid target in place of your plan.',['nccp']),
 item('Hearing, nerves and lung assessment','Cisplatin can affect hearing and nerves; vincristine can affect nerves and bowel function; lomustine can affect the lungs. Tell the team about changes before every visit. NCCP lists hearing and lung tests according to clinical need, while current lomustine product information advises baseline and continuing lung assessment. Ask which checks are booked for you.',['nccp','lomustine-smpc']),
 item('Brain and spine review','Medulloblastoma may involve the brain, spine or cerebrospinal fluid. Your specialist decides which imaging or other tests are needed at each stage. Keep the next scan date and result-review appointment in your passport. This guide does not set a universal scan, lumbar-puncture or blood tumour-marker timetable.',['nccp','nci-medulloblastoma']),
 item('Delayed effects and rehabilitation','Symptoms may change after surgery, RT or chemotherapy. Hearing, balance, strength, memory, fatigue and daily function deserve follow-up as well as scans. Ask which longer-term checks and rehabilitation are relevant after your particular treatment. Report new changes promptly rather than waiting for a routine appointment.',['nccp','nci-cns']),
 item('Keep results with decisions','Record when a test is booked, completed and explained, and the next agreed step. A normal result from one test does not replace another medicine-safety check. The team authorises treatment after considering symptoms, current results and earlier side effects.',['nccp'])]}
 # General symptom/support educational concepts are original wording and apply beyond glioma.
 for ch in cs[2:]:
  ch['id']=ch['id'].replace('glioma','brain-tumour')
  for it in ch['items']:
   it['source_ids']=['nccn-brain-support' if s=='nccn-patient' else s for s in it['source_ids']]
 return cs

